window.docContents[185].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.StatementPqOomFlag/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___StatementPqOomFlag":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Game › StatementPqOomFlag.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 177 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (10)def liftStateTdef liftQueryImplStateT2structure SMSchemeRMdef SMSchemeRM.initStatedef transmitRMdef challRMdef deliverRMdef injectRMdef oracleImplRMdef cliOracleImplRM\n\n\n\nMonadic lifting and SM game oracles for shared CLI / WriterT executionTrusted: the statement. Defines the monadic secure-messaging scheme SMSchemeRM and its R-game oracle handler oracleImplRM over [Monad M] [MonadLiftT ProbComp M]. StatementPq.lean instantiates M := ProbComp for cliPqExp, and StatementPqOomGame.lean instantiates M := WriterT (List Inputs) ProbComp for the input-logged game cliPqxdhExpFlagged; both share one driver and avoid classical decide inside ProbComp. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.\n\n\n\ndef liftStateTL35–38 ↗#Lift a StateT σ m computation along [MonadLiftT m n] (definitionally id at m = n).\n\ndef liftQueryImplStateT2L40–45 ↗#Lift an oracle handler on StateT σ₁ (StateT σ₂ m) along [MonadLiftT m n] (definitionally id at m = n).\n\nstructure SMSchemeRML47–54 ↗#Secure-messaging scheme with receive coins (SMSchemeR, DEV-LS1) whose send and receive run in a monad M.\n\ndef SMSchemeRM.initStateL56–62 ↗#Initial SM.GameState for key k and challenge bit b.\n\n\n\ndef transmitRML70–85 ↗#Monadic counterpart of SM.transmitR over StateT (SM.GameState St Msg C) M.\n\ndef challRML87–104 ↗#Monadic counterpart of SM.challR over StateT (SM.GameState St Msg C) M.\n\ndef deliverRML106–129 ↗#Monadic counterpart of SM.deliverR over StateT (SM.GameState St Msg C) M.\n\ndef injectRML131–151 ↗#Monadic counterpart of SM.injectR over StateT (SM.GameState St Msg C) M.\n\ndef oracleImplRML153–160 ↗#Combined R-game oracle handler (SM.oracleImplR) over StateT (SM.GameState St Msg C) M.\n\n\n\ndef cliOracleImplRML164–178 ↗#Monadic counterpart of cliOracleImplR: runs the R-game oracles on internal party state St' while projecting corr-P leakage along proj : St' → St (DEV-CLI18).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementPqOomFlag.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.StatementPqOomFlag/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___StatementPqOomFlag"},"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.StatementPqOomGame/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___StatementPqOomGame":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Game › StatementPqOomGame.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by no headline theorem 113 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Listed with the statement files, but no headline theorem uses it. None of its declarations is in the closure of a headline theorem of either proof. Tier 1 lists it, as the closure report does: the report lists every statement file (defaultStatementFiles in scripts/TrustedClosure.lean). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (8)def cliRunLoggeddef runCliDriverLoggeddef cliPqxdhExpFlaggeddef CliPqxdhFlagProbdef cliCoinsTape?def CliKemFailProbdef CliPqxdhExpFlaggedFaithfuldef CliPqBadProbVanishes\n\n\n\nInput-logged CLI security gameTrusted: the statement. Instantiates the monadic CLI game driver Dir.cliDrvImplM (StatementPq.lean) in WriterT (List Inputs) ProbComp via StatementPqOomFlag.lean so every Inputs record passed to run is appended to the writer log without classical decide inside ProbComp. Because WriterT sits beneath the game's StateT layers, logged inputs persist across calls that reject or leave party state unchanged. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.For any predicate bad : Inputs → Prop, CliPqxdhFlagProb is the probability under the logged experiment cliPqxdhExpFlagged that some call run i satisfies bad (used for excused aborts in StatementPqElf.lean). On the same log, CliKemFailProb is the probability that some ordered pair of logged 64-byte coins tapes forms a failing honest ML-KEM-768 exchange (MlKem.KemFailBad), which bounds adversary-chosen send randomness directly in the CLI game.\n\n\n\ndef cliRunLoggedL42–45 ↗#Append [i] to the WriterT log and return run i.\n\ndef runCliDriverLoggedL47–57 ↗#Run A against Dir.cliDrvImplM over WriterT (List Inputs) ProbComp with cliRunLogged run from the empty driver state.\n\ndef cliPqxdhExpFlaggedL59–71 ↗#Input-logged counterpart of cliPqExp in ProbComp (Bool × List Inputs).\n\ndef CliPqxdhFlagProbL73–78 ↗#Probability under cliPqxdhExpFlagged that at least one logged run input satisfies bad.\n\nML-KEM failure probability\n\ndef cliCoinsTape?L82–85 ↗#Contents of the last coinsFile entry in i (the entry read by the binary: 64 bytes on send, 32 on recv, 192 on init), or none if absent.\n\ndef CliKemFailProbL87–94 ↗#Probability in cliPqxdhExpFlagged that some ordered pair of logged 64-byte coins tapes forms a failing honest ML-KEM-768 exchange for W.Q.K (MlKem.KemFailBad).\n\nFaithfulness and vanishing-bad-event properties\n\ndef CliPqxdhExpFlaggedFaithfulL98–104 ↗#Projecting cliPqxdhExpFlagged onto its Bool outcome recovers the distribution of cliPqExp.\n\ndef CliPqBadProbVanishesL106–111 ↗#CliPqxdhFlagProb vanishes whenever bad holds on no input.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementPqOomGame.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.StatementPqOomGame/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___StatementPqOomGame"}});